#: b4b389137a8c4556876d8f0c817fcf86
msgid "Foundations"
msgstr ""

#: 5630713da5ce4a35b24c4e967d8dab4e
msgid ""
"Diátaxis is successful because it *works* - both users and creators have "
"a better experience of documentation as a result. It makes sense and it "
"feels right."
msgstr ""

#: ab4e7982dda440a3b476de3aaa1f038f
msgid ""
"However, that's not enough to be confident in Diátaxis as a theory of "
"documentation. As a theory, it needs to show *why* it works. It needs to "
"show that there is actually some reason why there are exactly four kinds "
"of documentation, not three or five. It needs to demonstrate rigorous "
"thinking and analysis, and that it stands on a sound theoretical "
"foundation."
msgstr ""

#: 6d0098ef18274db9aafa485ce64c7839
msgid ""
"Otherwise, it will be just another useful heuristic approach, and the "
"strongest claim we can make for it is that \"it seems to work quite "
"well\"."
msgstr ""

#: 9efa580e78fe45c292bc386f3be07b0e
msgid "Two dimensions of craft"
msgstr ""

#: 5664bce07a21462295f5ac1062b2c7f3
msgid ""
"Diátaxis is based on the principle that documentation must serve the "
"needs of its users. Knowing how to do that means understanding what the "
"needs of users are."
msgstr ""

#: 2da5ac0715f947148e2260a7af0b1042
msgid ""
"The user whose needs Diátaxis serves is *the practitioner in a domain of "
"skill*. A domain of skill is defined by a craft - the use of a tool or "
"product is a craft. So is an entire discipline or profession. Using a "
"programming language is a craft, as is flying a particular aircraft, or "
"even being a pilot in general."
msgstr ""

#: 0fa89def02904c4b8d9d740ca56eded1
msgid ""
"Understanding the needs of these users means in turn understanding the "
"essential characteristics of craft or skill."
msgstr ""

#: 9b262509d06b4c9e999ecc186885cf7f
msgid "Action/cognition"
msgstr ""

#: fafbd4cdad12498685a1e24814de46ed
msgid ""
"A skill or craft or practice contains both **action** (practical "
"knowledge, knowing *how*, what we do) and **cognition** (theoretical "
"knowledge, knowing *that*, what we think). The two are completely bound "
"up with each other, but they are counterparts, wholly distinct from each "
"other, two different aspects of the same thing."
msgstr ""

#: 7f9c3d28a552414d94f7e9e3271e3607
msgid "Acquisition/application"
msgstr ""

#: aff6f3ae246a4f4fb036887e16e03148
msgid ""
"Similarly, the relationship of a practitioner with their practice is that"
" it is something that needs to be both **acquired**, and **applied**. "
"Being \"at work\" (concerned with applying the skill and knowledge of "
"their craft) and being \"at study\" (concerned with acquiring them) are "
"once again counterparts, distinct but bound up with each other."
msgstr ""

#: e4147f5f2a694c68b3a6d95a06a9d2b3
msgid "The map of the territory"
msgstr ""

#: 20bda34e468540a5a19b9456d2fb7429
msgid ""
"This gives us two dimensions of skill, that we can lay out on a map - a "
"map of the territory of craft:"
msgstr ""

#: 03a971e2da3041bd8d207ede0ee970fa c28f7e16c62a46188475162fa53653a7
msgid "The territory of craft as a two-dimensional map"
msgstr ""

#: c4c0b6354a704ed5850b8d24b18a3b68
msgid ""
"This is a *complete* map. There are only two dimensions, and they don't "
"just cover the entire territory, they define it. This is why there are "
"necessarily four quarters to it, and there could not be three, or five. "
"It is not an arbitrary number."
msgstr ""

#: 8a24d0e7860c4745ab4e7b85d8eb1d1e
msgid ""
"It also shows us the *qualities* of craft that define each of them. When "
"the idea that documentation must serve the needs of craft is applied to "
"this map, it reveals in turn what documentation must be and do to fulfil "
"those obligations - in four distinct ways."
msgstr ""

#: e8ee372740f546c6865a1d6280d13c01
msgid "Serving needs"
msgstr ""

#: e00a65e784c9480a9618cff80921359a
msgid ""
"The map of the territory of craft is what gives us the familiar Diátaxis "
"map of documentation. The map is in effect an answer to the question: "
"what must documentation do to align with these qualities of skill, and to"
" what need is it oriented in each case?"
msgstr ""

#: 06c07725e21443a8b4bba0d6507c8991
msgid ""
"We can see how the map of documentation addresses *needs* across those "
"two dimensions, each need also defined by the characteristics of its "
"quarter of the map."
msgstr ""

